WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.150
If you've seen Avengers: Endgame, now's a
good time to start unpacking exactly how the

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.620
MCU will cope with its losses, what those
deaths mean for our heroes, and how future

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.900
stories will be affected.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:15.680
If you haven't seen the film yet, consider
this your first, second, and final warning:

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.500
Major spoilers ahead!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:23.500
Marvel's Infinity Saga started with Tony Stark,
so it's only fitting that it ends with him.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.560
If Tony Stark had to die, we're glad he got
to go out the way he did.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.300
After declaring "I am Iron Man" right in Thanos'
face, he snaps the Mad Titan and his whole

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.010
army from existence.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.430
Of course, everyone is absolutely devastated
in the aftermath of Tony's death, as we see

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.360
at the funeral for the Armored Avenger.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.570
Pretty much every surviving superhero was
in attendance, and it's clear that the loss

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.570
will echo throughout the community for years
to come, particularly when it comes to those

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.260
closest to him, like Peter Parker and Nick
Fury.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.860
And then there's Tony's family.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.520
Happy Hogan is clearly stepping in to be a
kind of father figure to Morgan Stark, promising

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.060
to buy her all the cheeseburgers she wants,
but Pepper Potts' grief will run deeper.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.640
After years of worrying about him, she could
see that Tony really was at peace after ending

00:01:11.659 --> 00:01:13.289
his own personal curse.

00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:18.080
Still, she'll miss him every day, even if
we never see this portrayed in future films.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.220
Black Widow was one of the MCU's great survivors.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.060
She faced down countless superpowered threats
and personal demons throughout her life, and

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.320
at least her death was on her own terms.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.080
"This is gonna work, Steve."

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:31.920
"I know it is.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.880
'Cause I don't know what I'm gonna do if it
doesn't."

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:39.400
Natasha Romkanoff chose to sacrifice herself
so that her fellow Avengers could get on with

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.180
their lives.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.860
As she said all along: She had red in her
ledger, and this was the ultimate way of wiping

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:45.640
that out.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:49.080
Sadly, Natasha didn't get a funeral, at least
not that we saw.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:53.479
Her death came during the Avengers' epic time
heist, and we saw the grief in the faces of

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.000
her comrades as they swore to make her loss
worth it.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.720
Beyond the emotional loss, there's also a
greater loss for the MCU.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.680
In the face of everything, Natasha was always
the cool one under pressure.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.700
She became the field commander for the Avengers
in the years after the Decimation, and the

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.260
point of contact for heroes all over the galaxy.

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:14.060
Now someone else will need to fill her shoes,
and it'll be hard to find someone who's up

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:14.940
to the task.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.180
Tony Stark is gone, but the technology he
brought into the world is not.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:25.230
His inventions have heavily impacted the MCU,
and two other superheroes proudly wear his

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:30.189
tech: There's War Machine and now there's
Pepper Potts, who suits up in her own armor,

00:02:30.189 --> 00:02:32.960
taking on an identity that Marvel Comics calls
"Rescue."

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.460
Though it's unlikely that Gwyneth Paltrow
will return to the MCU, War Machine will probably

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:38.780
still be knocking around.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.200
And Stark's Iron Man suits won't be going
anywhere in the public imagination, particularly

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.200
after he saved the world in such spectacular
fashion.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:50.659
With that in mind, it might be time to call
up a young scientist to fill Stark's shoes

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.260
and take flight in his suits.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.960
In the comics, there's a teenager named Riri
Williams, who wears Stark-style armor and

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.520
calls herself "Ironheart."

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.280
Some fans have speculated that Black Panther's
little sister Shuri could take on this particular

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:04.940
mantle in the MCU.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:08.920
But perhaps it'll be Stark's daughter Morgan,
or a character haven't spent much time with.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.880
Whatever the case, the MCU is ripe for new
blood, and Ironheart could lead the charge.

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:15.820
"Maybe."

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.930
With his last act of heroism, Tony Stark not
only killed Thanos, but wiped away every last

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.700
trace of his minions and soldiers, ridding
the universe of its greatest threat.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:31.200
In the first Avengers film, the character
known only as the Other gave Thanos a sharply-worded

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.420
warning about fighting the heroes of Earth.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:40.960
"To challenge them is to court death."

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.980
Thanos simply smiled at the words, which is
so Thanos, and, at the time, it seemed like

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:50.269
a wink to the audience members who knew that
comic book Thanos had a massive crush on the

00:03:50.269 --> 00:03:54.040
bony lady known as Death, and he literally
wanted to court her.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.750
But now that Endgame has come and gone, and
the Other's warning has been proven with the

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:02.320
death of Thanos, that only heightens the cosmic
reputation of the Earth and its heroes.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.900
There's a whole universe out there, and it
all went through the Decimation.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:09.540
As everyone recovers, word will spread of
the heroes of Earth and how they were the

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:11.700
key to undoing all of Thanos' work.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:15.140
That means future supervillains are even more
likely to fear Earth.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.400
It also means there's a massive power vacuum
that used to be filled with Thanos and his

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.080
minions.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.580
Yes, the universe's greatest threat is gone,
but power vacuums have to be filled on both

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.580
sides of the good and evil divide.

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.520
Somewhere out there, some madman or madwoman
is hellbent on destruction, eager to get a

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.300
taste of the Avengers and prove they can beat
them.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.960
As Vision said, this kind of power is bound
to invite confrontation.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.920
As part of the entrance of Riri Williams as
Ironheart in the Marvel Comics universe, it

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.900
was revealed that Tony Stark sustained such
serious injuries in the Civil War II event

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:49.280
that he fell into a coma.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:54.199
But he conveniently made a copy of his consciousness
beforehand, which was able to assist Riri

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.120
and freely chat with other Marvel characters
as a form of artificial intelligence.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:02.500
This Tony Stark A.I. became a mainstay of
the Marvel Universe, and retained all the

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.810
wit and wisdom that characterized Tony.

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:08.540
Tony's last recording for his daughter is
just that, a recording.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:13.020
But considering everything Tony has tinkered
with over the years, including frequent artificial

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:16.889
intelligence ventures, it's quite possible
that he would have taken a cue from his comics

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:20.510
counterpart and found some way to record himself
as a consciousness.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:26.040
"Hey Miss Potts, if you find this recording,
don't feel bad about this."

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:30.400
This would allow the character to carry on
in some form, and it would create opportunities

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:35.190
for Robert Downey Jr. to continue making cameos
in any upcoming MCU projects.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:39.490
Tony Stark the man would be gone, but Tony
Stark the artificial intelligence could live

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.760
on... if only as a voice in another hero's
head.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.180
And an extremely sassy voice, at that.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.600
"We're going out of town."

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:46.840
"Okay, we've been through this, nope."

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:47.440
"Yup.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.300
"The man says no."

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.580
"Immediately and indefinitely."

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:50.080
"Honey."

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:50.740
"Great idea."

